SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Chamfers: the corner where four or more planar chamfers meet round a
vertex, their sections there in one plane, is that plane; fillets and
chamfers of a solid whose own orientation is reversed (mitcad#2306, a
case of a public B-rep benchmark, mitcad#2273, GitHub mitcad/Mitcad#576).

The case: the octahedron |x| + |y| + |z| <= 10, all twelve edges
chamfered sqrt(6) on both faces. Four chamfers meet at each vertex; each
is a plane, and the contact lines of two neighbours cross on their common
face, where each chamfer's section at the vertex ends: four straight
segments bounding a square in one plane (x = 6 at the vertex (10, 0, 0)).
Traced in DRAW: the stripes build, and at every vertex
PerformMoreThreeCorner finds the four crossings and puts the four
sections into its plate as borders held G1 to each chamfer's surface. No
surface is tangent to the four planes along the square's sides: the
plate is not done at any of the six vertices, every vertex is faulty and
the chamfer is not done.

- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformMoreThreeCorner: where every edge at the vertex
  is chamfered (no sharp edge), each chamfer's surface data at the corner
  is a plane that meets both its neighbours on the faces between them,
  and the sections lie in one plane within the approximation tolerance
  (SectionsOfChamfersInOnePlane), the plate is built G0 to the sections;
  where the plane it starts from holds every end of the sections and the
  plate's curves end at them, within the same tolerance (CornerPlane),
  that plane is the corner's surface instead of the plate's
  approximation, with the plate's curves on it. Elsewhere nothing
  changes.

The case's test makes the octahedron as the solid of its sewn shell,
which faces in, oriented by BRepLib::OrientClosedSolid, which reverses
the solid. Every fillet or chamfer of a solid whose own orientation is
reversed came out invalid: the result is rebuilt in new solids, which
took the input solid's shells without its own orientation, so every face
of the input the blends did not make faced in (the octahedron's eight
triangles; a box's faces beside one chamfered edge, its volume
negative).

- ChFi3d_Builder::ChFi3d_Builder: a solid whose own orientation is
  reversed is taken as the same solid oriented forward holding its shells
  with that orientation composed into theirs (ForwardSolid): the same
  faces, each with the orientation it has within the solid given. Any
  other shape as before.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 2306.
